# ---- Atmosphere frontend configuration ----
# Copy to .env to override. In development you usually need NOTHING here — the
# Vite dev server proxies /api to the backend (http://localhost:4000) so the
# browser talks to a single origin and cookies work automatically.

# Backend origin used by the dev-server proxy (see vite.config.ts).
# VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:4000

# ---- Technician app: object detection ----
# The COCO-SSD weights (~18 MB) are fetched from Google's CDN on first use and
# then served from the browser cache. Point this at a self-hosted model.json to
# avoid the third-party dependency — required on networks that block the CDN,
# and worth doing for an air-gapped deployment. Copy model.json and its
# group1-shard* files from
#   https://storage.googleapis.com/tfjs-models/savedmodel/ssdlite_mobilenet_v2/
# into e.g. frontend/public/models/coco-ssd/ and set:
# VITE_COCO_SSD_MODEL_URL=/models/coco-ssd/model.json

# In PRODUCTION, if the backend is served from a different origin than the
# frontend, set its absolute base URL here (e.g. https://api.atmosphere.app).
# Requests then go directly there with credentials. Leave empty when the
# backend is reverse-proxied under the same origin at /api.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
